NAME
        manipulate - change the content of the fields of a header

SYNOPSIS
        manipulate <type> header 
        manipulate <type> header <field>:<value>

DESCRIPTION
        Change the values of the fields of a header you are carrying. Making 
        sure your headers are in order is necessary if you wish to get 
        anywhere in the network. Various computers, systems and devices will
        only accept you if your fields have the expected content.

        What is the right content? You will have to be creative and find out
        for your selves.
         
OPTIONS
 	<type>  - the type of header you wish to manipulate. You need to be
                  carrying the header in order to manipulate it.
        <field> - the specific field you wish to manipulate, either specifying
                  its name or its place in the header (starting with 1 in the
                  upper left corner of the header). 
                  Leaving field and value unspecified lists the avaliable 
                  fields and their descriptions.
        <value> - The value you wish to set the field to. In most cases this
                  is just an integer value of some size. But some field might
                  have a different format in which case that format should
                  be used when specifying the value.
	
SEE ALSO
	network, status, headers
